      "farewell": "Wrote `answer_1034131706.preql` and it runs cleanly:\n\n```\nimport root.Claim_Coverage as cc;\nselect cc.Policy_Coverage_Detail.Policy.policy_number as policy_number,\n       count(cc.claim_identifier) as claim_count\norder by policy_number asc;\n```\n\nResult (claims placed per policy number):\n- 31003000336 \u2192 2\n- 31003000337 \u2192 0\n\nHow I got there: the `Claim` model has no declared relationship to `Policy`, so the claim\u2194policy bridge is `Claim_Coverage` (grain = one row per claim, `claim_identifier`), which has a declared FK `Policy_Coverage_Detail_Identifier` to `Policy_Coverage_Detail`, which in turn joins to `Policy`. I verified the join shape with a `--dry-run` (the generated SQL joins `Claim_Coverage` to `Policy_Coverage_Detail` on that identifier and then to `Policy` on `Policy_Identifier`). Counting claims per policy number gives 2 for policy 31003000336 and 0 for 31003000337 (the model keeps all policy members).",
